1
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:21,350
Let's do this every day.

2
00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:41,110
Dance with me, honey.

3
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,070
What?

4
00:00:42,070 --> 00:00:43,600
Didn't they take good care of you?

5
00:00:43,790 --> 00:00:45,470
Do you know what I like about you?

6
00:00:46,430 --> 00:00:48,150
Your hands are just like mine.

7
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:49,350
Neither of us has clean hands.

8
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:26,140
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 5=

9
00:01:37,590 --> 00:01:38,400
What's going on?

10
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,280
Captain Qin.

11
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,310
A villager reported to our station.

12
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:42,280
He said the soil in his vegetable patch

13
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:43,640
looked like it had been freshly dug up.

14
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:46,120
He also found
what looked like spots of blood nearby.

15
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,350
We did a preliminary examination.

16
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:49,040
Just give me the results.

17
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:51,040
The preliminary blood test

18
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:51,920
came back positive.

19
00:01:52,230 --> 00:01:53,510
We suspect a body was buried here.

20
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:54,870
I didn't dare let them dig any further.

21
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:56,920
Let's take a look.

22
00:01:57,070 --> 00:01:57,870
This way.

23
00:02:00,150 --> 00:02:02,040
Captain, the blood was found here.

24
00:02:16,190 --> 00:02:17,560
Those are resettlement apartments
across the way, right?

25
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:18,360
Yes.

26
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:19,360
They were just completed recently.

27
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:20,630
Not many people live there yet.

28
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,150
When the villager reported it,

29
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:23,750
did he give an exact location?

30
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:24,590
No.

31
00:02:24,590 --> 00:02:25,870
He only said he found blood

32
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:27,430
and signs that the soil
had been disturbed.

33
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:28,080
Yes.

34
00:02:28,310 --> 00:02:29,120
Li.

35
00:02:30,430 --> 00:02:31,240
Take some men.

36
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:32,430
Split up and search.

37
00:02:32,470 --> 00:02:33,280
Hurry.

38
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:34,310
Guys,

39
00:02:34,310 --> 00:02:35,310
split up and search.

40
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:37,030
The captain said to hurry.

41
00:02:37,030 --> 00:02:37,680
Let's go.

42
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,680
You too.

43
00:02:40,310 --> 00:02:41,470
Spit out that flower.

44
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,430
Don't all crowd together.

45
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:00,000
You two, check over there.

46
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,080
Captain Qin.

47
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:09,120
I found it!

48
00:03:17,190 --> 00:03:18,310
A white... White-haired corpse.

49
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:19,280
Captain Qin.

50
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:20,120
It's a white-haired corpse.

51
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,750
Medical Examiner Zhou once said

52
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:25,470
white-haired corpses usually form in

53
00:03:25,470 --> 00:03:26,960
damp, enclosed spaces.

54
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:28,870
The exposed areas
and even the entire body

55
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:30,870
may develop these white fungal patches

56
00:03:30,870 --> 00:03:31,710
or mold filaments.

57
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:34,030
But these mold filaments
are incredibly long.

58
00:03:34,030 --> 00:03:35,430
Captain Qin, be careful.

59
00:03:39,470 --> 00:03:39,960
Captain Qin.

60
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:42,000
Don't touch me!

61
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:44,360
All you're good at is eating.

62
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,430
You're useless at everything else.

63
00:03:56,630 --> 00:03:57,430
Li.

64
00:03:57,750 --> 00:03:58,520
Come here.

65
00:03:58,520 --> 00:03:59,280
Come over here.

66
00:03:59,430 --> 00:04:00,240
Come on.

67
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:03,800
What's this?

68
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,680
Why is it a dog?

69
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:09,800
I thought it was a body.

70
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,560
Keep digging.

71
00:04:12,430 --> 00:04:13,750
That scared me just now.

72
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:14,560
Wait.

73
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:16,870
Who would bury a dog here?

74
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,870
Judging by its size,

75
00:04:27,390 --> 00:04:28,630
it must weigh over 40 pounds.

76
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,040
There's bleeding around the throat.

77
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,190
It was probably killed
by having its throat cut.

78
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:35,600
Yesterday, a little girl
in our jurisdiction filed a report.

79
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,650
She said her dog was missing.

80
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:38,190
(Generous Reward for Missing Dog)
It was a white, long-haired dog.

81
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:39,000
Looks like this is the one.

82
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:39,480
Maomao.

83
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,870
Mommy can't find you.

84
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:47,220
(Generous Reward for Missing Dog)

85
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:49,070
Find the girl tomorrow
and have her identify it.

86
00:04:49,070 --> 00:04:49,400
Yes.

87
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:49,950
Qin.

88
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,040
Zhou.

89
00:04:51,190 --> 00:04:51,750
Chief Zhao.

90
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:52,270
Zhou.

91
00:04:52,270 --> 00:04:53,040
Thanks for your hard work.

92
00:04:53,560 --> 00:04:54,560
What's the situation here?

93
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:56,000
A local resident reported

94
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:57,630
finding blood in this area.

95
00:04:58,510 --> 00:04:59,750
But when we came over,

96
00:05:01,270 --> 00:05:02,390
we dug this up.

97
00:05:02,390 --> 00:05:03,920
The preliminary blood test was positive.

98
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,360
How did we end up digging up a dog?

99
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:06,480
Could the test be wrong?

100
00:05:06,630 --> 00:05:07,720
That's not unusual.

101
00:05:07,870 --> 00:05:09,950
A preliminary blood test
mainly determines

102
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:11,360
whether a stain is actually blood.

103
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:13,240
To determine whether it's human blood

104
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,390
or blood from another animal,

105
00:05:14,390 --> 00:05:15,870
we need to run
a species identification test.

106
00:05:16,430 --> 00:05:17,240
Chief Zhao.

107
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,720
There's something I don't understand.

108
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:21,310
Why would the person who killed this dog

109
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:23,270
go to all this trouble

110
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:25,070
to bury it here?

111
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:28,070
Could it be

112
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,750
that someone's
trying to cover something up?

113
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:32,000
Or

114
00:05:32,190 --> 00:05:34,040
trying to divert our attention?

115
00:05:36,070 --> 00:05:36,870
Could it be...

116
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:38,430
You mean...

117
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:40,750
I have a bad feeling about this.

118
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:54,950
Zhou.

119
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:57,160
Did you bring
a magnifying glass and tweezers?

120
00:05:57,630 --> 00:05:58,240
Here.

121
00:06:12,390 --> 00:06:13,120
Tweezers.

122
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,040
Here.

123
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,040
I'll hold the light for you.

124
00:06:24,430 --> 00:06:25,040
Hair.

125
00:06:25,270 --> 00:06:26,870
Li, keep digging.

126
00:06:27,270 --> 00:06:27,830
Dig.

127
00:06:38,830 --> 00:06:39,630
Qin.

128
00:06:39,750 --> 00:06:40,680
Are you sure about this?

129
00:06:42,190 --> 00:06:43,560
I don't know if I'm sure.

130
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:45,830
But if anything happens,
you'll have to back me up.

131
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,630
We found something!

132
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,270
Quick.

133
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,390
Quick!

134
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:56,310
We've got a problem.

135
00:06:59,360 --> 00:07:00,870
Looks like the tip
from the public was right.

136
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,390
Someone used the dog's body

137
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,000
to conceal a human body.

138
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,040
The killer was probably
afraid the freshly disturbed soil

139
00:07:06,040 --> 00:07:07,190
would attract attention,

140
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:09,000
so they buried a dog on top of the body.

141
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,480
That way, they could
delay us from finding the body.

142
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:17,600
Take it slow.

143
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,560
Don't damage the body.

144
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,270
I'll do it.

145
00:07:34,830 --> 00:07:35,680
This face...

146
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:39,600
I feel like I've seen her
somewhere before.

147
00:07:40,950 --> 00:07:41,750
Captain Qin.

148
00:07:42,390 --> 00:07:43,360
You know her?

149
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,190
I'm not sure.

150
00:07:44,310 --> 00:07:45,720
Maybe I've mistaken her
for someone else.

151
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:48,270
Once the autopsy is done,

152
00:07:48,480 --> 00:07:50,310
send out a composite
and her identifying features

153
00:07:50,310 --> 00:07:51,630
and check them against missing persons.

154
00:07:51,630 --> 00:07:52,390
Also,

155
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:54,120
the soles of her shoes

156
00:07:54,190 --> 00:07:56,070
were unusually clean at the scene.

157
00:07:56,070 --> 00:07:58,360
And both heels

158
00:07:58,510 --> 00:08:01,040
showed clear signs of friction
from a sloped surface.

159
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:07,800
I see.

160
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:08,800
Come here.

161
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:12,830
See that?

162
00:08:13,190 --> 00:08:14,920
If someone is dragged
for a long distance,

163
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:16,800
the shape of the worn heel

164
00:08:16,870 --> 00:08:18,360
would match
the shoes on the victim's feet

165
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:19,920
exactly like this.

166
00:08:26,270 --> 00:08:27,070
Got it.

167
00:08:27,070 --> 00:08:28,560
Qin, let me also tell you

168
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:30,920
what we've found
from the external examination.

169
00:08:31,510 --> 00:08:34,080
The victim
was about 170 centimeters tall

170
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:36,000
and weighed around 50 kilograms.

171
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:37,630
Judging by her appearance,

172
00:08:37,630 --> 00:08:39,390
she was probably around 30 years old.

173
00:08:39,390 --> 00:08:42,150
Her fingernails and toenails
were painted red.

174
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,600
And judging
from the entire surface of the body,

175
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,320
there were no open wounds.

176
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:48,120
So the fresh blood at the scene

177
00:08:48,120 --> 00:08:49,550
probably came from the dog.

178
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:52,960
The body shows
no signs of decomposition.

179
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:54,030
The corneas are cloudy,

180
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:55,510
and the pupils are no longer visible.

181
00:08:55,630 --> 00:08:57,840
The lividity
doesn't blanch under pressure.

182
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,510
Rigor mortis has also begun

183
00:08:59,510 --> 00:09:00,630
to subside.

184
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:02,670
This indicates that she died

185
00:09:02,670 --> 00:09:03,960
between 24

186
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:05,550
and 48 hours ago.

187
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:06,390
Zhou.

188
00:09:06,390 --> 00:09:07,510
I don't mean to interrupt you.

189
00:09:07,510 --> 00:09:08,790
There's too much going on at the bureau,

190
00:09:09,030 --> 00:09:10,790
so we don't need every detail right now.

191
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,360
What we're most concerned about is

192
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:14,320
whether there are signs
of sexual assault

193
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:16,390
or murder.

194
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:17,510
When she was found,

195
00:09:17,510 --> 00:09:18,510
her underwear was intact,

196
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:19,960
and there was no injury
to the perineal area.

197
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,600
The preliminary semen test was negative.

198
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,670
So there's no evidence
of sexual assault.

199
00:09:23,670 --> 00:09:24,480
However,

200
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:27,550
the clasp on the back
of her bra had been torn off.

201
00:09:27,550 --> 00:09:30,270
And on the inner sides of both ankles,

202
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:32,240
there were patches
of subcutaneous bleeding.

203
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,840
The skin on both her hands

204
00:09:34,030 --> 00:09:36,960
showed parallel strips of abrasion.

205
00:09:37,030 --> 00:09:39,600
The proximal joint of her
right middle finger was dislocated.

206
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:40,480
Taken together,

207
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:42,510
these still don't prove
she was murdered.

208
00:09:42,510 --> 00:09:43,630
But I believe

209
00:09:43,910 --> 00:09:45,390
the body never lies.

210
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:47,510
Have you identified the victim?

211
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,910
We've already
sent people to investigate.

212
00:09:48,910 --> 00:09:49,600
Good.

213
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,320
Zhou.

214
00:09:50,550 --> 00:09:51,360
Please get the autopsy report

215
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,910
to the office tomorrow.

216
00:09:52,910 --> 00:09:53,720
We'll get going.

217
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:54,360
All right.

218
00:09:57,150 --> 00:09:57,960
Let's continue.

219
00:09:58,340 --> 00:10:00,460
(White-Haired Female Corpse Case)

220
00:10:00,550 --> 00:10:01,360
Qin.

221
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:02,550
Qin.

222
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:03,910
I found another unsolved case
from the '90s

223
00:10:03,910 --> 00:10:05,600
in the archives.

224
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:10,600
You're looking at this too?

225
00:10:11,510 --> 00:10:13,120
I'm also looking
at the White-Haired Female Corpse Case.

226
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:14,320
(White-Haired Female Corpse Case)
Are you sure

227
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:16,510
this has always been
an unsolved case in the archives?

228
00:10:16,510 --> 00:10:17,910
I've read about this case too.

229
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,630
I even studied it before.

230
00:10:19,670 --> 00:10:20,840
Because it's such an unusual case.

231
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:21,910
It involved both a person and a dog.

232
00:10:22,150 --> 00:10:23,480
How do all of you know about it?

233
00:10:23,670 --> 00:10:24,390
This clearly...

234
00:10:24,390 --> 00:10:25,150
Right.

235
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:27,440
This really is one of Longfan City's

236
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:28,750
most famous unsolved cases.

237
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,000
This case

238
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,510
also dates back to 1990.

239
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,200
I came across it by chance.

240
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:35,120
I just don't know
if there's any useful information.

241
00:10:37,150 --> 00:10:37,720
Look.

242
00:10:40,150 --> 00:10:41,360
This is all the information there is.

243
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,100
It was 1990.

244
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:45,010
There were no surveillance cameras,
and forensic technology was limited.

245
00:10:45,360 --> 00:10:46,870
With a cold case like this,

246
00:10:46,870 --> 00:10:48,750
they couldn't even
find a viable suspect.

247
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:54,720
You want to investigate this case?

248
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,080
I don't know how to explain this to you.

249
00:11:03,150 --> 00:11:04,840
This really isn't an unsolved case.

250
00:11:04,870 --> 00:11:05,750
But what if I told you

251
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:06,750
this happened just yesterday?

252
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:07,630
Would you believe me?

253
00:11:07,870 --> 00:11:10,750
Then if this isn't an unsolved case,

254
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:13,270
what kind of case is it?

255
00:11:15,030 --> 00:11:15,840
A cold case?

256
00:11:17,150 --> 00:11:17,960
Qin Ming.

257
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:20,840
What's wrong?

258
00:11:27,220 --> 00:11:31,340
(People's Republic of China Police)

259
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:33,780
(Forensic Pathology Report)

260
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,550
You scared me.

261
00:11:45,670 --> 00:11:46,630
What are you doing?

262
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,200
I knew you wouldn't be here alone.

263
00:11:51,790 --> 00:11:54,200
Didn't I say I'd bring it over tomorrow?

264
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:55,630
The bureau couldn't wait.

265
00:11:55,630 --> 00:11:56,960
Are the results out yet?

266
00:11:58,630 --> 00:12:00,120
They just came out.

267
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:02,780
(Forensic Pathology Report)
Here, take a look.

268
00:12:02,790 --> 00:12:03,870
The victim

269
00:12:03,870 --> 00:12:06,360
had a comminuted fracture
of the right upper arm.

270
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:08,200
A single bone
was broken into several pieces.

271
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:10,840
She also had multiple rib fractures
in the lower back.

272
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:13,150
The broken ends pierced
directly into the chest cavity.

273
00:12:13,510 --> 00:12:16,030
Her lungs, liver,
and spleen were all ruptured.

274
00:12:16,030 --> 00:12:18,000
There was extensive bleeding
in the chest and abdominal cavities.

275
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,000
The cause of death was hemorrhagic shock

276
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
and traumatic shock
from multiple injuries.

277
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:26,080
I see.

278
00:12:26,630 --> 00:12:27,720
You scared me again.

279
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:31,600
There's a main road
near where the body was found.

280
00:12:32,390 --> 00:12:33,960
Could it be a hit-and-run?

281
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:36,030
I don't think it was a hit-and-run.

282
00:12:36,270 --> 00:12:38,440
Injuries from traffic accidents
have obvious

283
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,390
abrasions.

284
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,870
But the victim's injuries
were all caused by impact,

285
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:42,860
with one side more severely injured.

286
00:12:42,860 --> 00:12:44,300
The external injuries were minor,
but the internal injuries were severe.

287
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:46,080
A single impact could have caused them.

288
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:46,910
Zhou.

289
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,600
Could she have fallen from a height?

290
00:12:52,030 --> 00:12:54,720
I believe she died
from a fall while still alive.

291
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,200
That makes sense.

292
00:13:09,150 --> 00:13:11,630
You're just having
rice soaked in vegetable broth?

293
00:13:12,670 --> 00:13:13,510
I'm used to it.

294
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:15,510
I don't like eating vegetables.

295
00:13:19,750 --> 00:13:20,600
Zhou.

296
00:13:21,270 --> 00:13:22,720
This is why I say you're good.

297
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,000
There was something
I just couldn't figure out.

298
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,240
That female victim

299
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:27,720
clearly showed
no signs of sexual assault.

300
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:30,320
So why was the clasp
on her bra torn off?

301
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:32,240
Then you said she fell from a height.

302
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:33,390
That could explain it too.

303
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,870
It suddenly occurred to me.

304
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:36,720
The killer must have

305
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,910
pushed the victim from a height,

306
00:13:39,080 --> 00:13:41,360
then dragged her
to that vacant lot and buried her.

307
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:43,270
There aren't any high-rise buildings
around that lot.

308
00:13:43,270 --> 00:13:43,870
Right.

309
00:13:43,870 --> 00:13:45,200
There aren't any tall buildings nearby.

310
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,120
So we can basically conclude

311
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:48,150
that someone transported her there.

312
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:50,480
The fact that the soles
of her shoes were so clean

313
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:51,750
also supports that conclusion.

314
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:53,360
So I think

315
00:13:53,870 --> 00:13:55,630
our first step now

316
00:13:56,030 --> 00:13:57,390
is to find where she fell

317
00:13:58,150 --> 00:14:00,000
and identify the primary crime scene.

318
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,670
Only then can we

319
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:02,550
reconstruct what happened.

320
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:03,240
Right?

321
00:14:03,270 --> 00:14:04,080
Captain Qin.

322
00:14:04,860 --> 00:14:06,490
We've confirmed the identity
of the white-haired female corpse.

323
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:09,360
She's the suspect
we've been looking for.

324
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:10,150
Jin Juan.

325
00:14:10,390 --> 00:14:11,480
- Jin Juan?
- Jin Juan?

326
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:14,150
That body is Jin Juan?

327
00:14:18,910 --> 00:14:20,080
Huo Qicheng just died,

328
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,630
and now the prime suspect in his case

329
00:14:21,630 --> 00:14:22,480
is dead too.

330
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:24,480
This can't be a coincidence.

331
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:25,840
Li.

332
00:14:26,270 --> 00:14:27,120
Here's what I want you to do.

333
00:14:27,390 --> 00:14:28,750
Go through
all of Huo Qicheng and Jin Juan's

334
00:14:28,750 --> 00:14:29,670
social connections again,

335
00:14:29,670 --> 00:14:30,880
as well as everyone

336
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:33,670
who had a grudge against
Longfan Urban Construction Group.

337
00:14:33,670 --> 00:14:34,840
Screen them all again.

338
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:36,440
There has to be something we can find.

339
00:14:46,670 --> 00:14:47,670
- Have you eaten?
- Have you eaten?

340
00:14:50,630 --> 00:14:51,440
Qin.

341
00:14:51,670 --> 00:14:52,440
Qin, can you hear me?

342
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,120
Qin.

343
00:14:53,440 --> 00:14:55,120
Qin, respond if you can hear me.

344
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,120
I'm here. I hear you.

345
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:56,960
You brat.

346
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:58,750
Is there another development
in the case?

347
00:14:58,910 --> 00:14:59,720
Yes.

348
00:15:00,390 --> 00:15:01,480
I saw the case file.

349
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:02,550
Jin Juan is dead.

350
00:15:02,870 --> 00:15:05,030
We've also just confirmed
Jin Juan's death.

351
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:06,510
Does the case file you have

352
00:15:06,510 --> 00:15:08,870
contain any useful leads?

353
00:15:09,270 --> 00:15:10,390
It's an unsolved case.

354
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,080
There's nothing useful in the file.

355
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:13,870
But I noticed the file mentioned

356
00:15:13,870 --> 00:15:15,000
two bodies.

357
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:15,960
Besides the human body,

358
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:17,080
there was also a dog's body.

359
00:15:17,080 --> 00:15:18,910
But there was no autopsy record
for the dog.

360
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:19,870
Qin.

361
00:15:20,030 --> 00:15:21,720
You should take another look
at the dog's body.

362
00:15:22,030 --> 00:15:23,120
Perform an autopsy on a dog?

363
00:15:23,510 --> 00:15:24,320
We've

364
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:26,080
never done that before.

365
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:27,080
We have a rule here.

366
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,720
No body gets overlooked.

367
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:29,480
The dog, just like the person,

368
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:30,750
was deliberately killed.

369
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:32,870
Its body, just like a human body,

370
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:33,910
can tell us what happened.

371
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:34,910
All right, I understand.

372
00:15:34,910 --> 00:15:35,910
I'll go take a look first.

373
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:41,900
(White-Haired Female Corpse
Found in City Outskirts)

374
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:43,870
You're back.

375
00:15:45,270 --> 00:15:46,080
Dad.

376
00:15:46,510 --> 00:15:49,270
Mom and I bought
lots of groceries today.

377
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,440
Mom said

378
00:15:50,870 --> 00:15:53,510
she's making your favorite
braised fish tonight.

379
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:54,320
Mom's the best.

380
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:55,270
Dad will be back soon, okay?

381
00:15:55,270 --> 00:15:56,360
I just need to take care
of something first.

382
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:57,960
You're going out again?

383
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:58,750
The case is urgent.

384
00:15:59,000 --> 00:15:59,910
I have to go.

385
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:02,270
Have a little something first.

386
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:03,440
All right, I got it.

387
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:05,390
Once things settle down,
I'll spend time with you both.

388
00:16:06,270 --> 00:16:07,150
I'm heading out.

389
00:16:07,390 --> 00:16:08,440
I forgot to tell you.

390
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:09,960
Our son,

391
00:16:10,080 --> 00:16:11,270
just wait and see.

392
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:11,910
He

393
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:12,790
is going to be

394
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:13,550
someone important someday.

395
00:16:13,550 --> 00:16:14,320
Really something.

396
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:15,510
Be careful.

397
00:16:17,510 --> 00:16:18,510
Someone important.

398
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:19,910
Come on.

399
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:20,750
Let's go make the fish.

400
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:23,630
If that girl finds out

401
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:25,030
we dug up the family member

402
00:16:25,030 --> 00:16:25,870
she just buried,

403
00:16:25,870 --> 00:16:27,080
she'll come after us for sure.

404
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:28,270
Captain Qin said

405
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:30,150
that girl would want to know even more

406
00:16:30,150 --> 00:16:31,550
who killed her dog.

407
00:16:31,750 --> 00:16:32,510
We're doing this

408
00:16:32,510 --> 00:16:33,960
to help her find the killer.

409
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:34,790
Keep digging.

410
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:35,630
All right.

411
00:16:55,870 --> 00:16:56,670
Li.

412
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,360
It wasn't killed
by having its throat cut.

413
00:16:58,910 --> 00:16:59,550
Look.

414
00:17:00,150 --> 00:17:01,080
Its head

415
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:03,360
was smashed apart by something.

416
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:05,070
Should we

417
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:07,200
do an autopsy
and determine the cause of death?

418
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:07,960
Don't rush.

419
00:17:08,030 --> 00:17:09,000
We'll take it step by step.

420
00:17:09,070 --> 00:17:10,590
This is my first time doing this too.

421
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,830
A curved laceration.

422
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,000
The wound edges are clean.

423
00:17:18,550 --> 00:17:19,920
There's also a clearly defined

424
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:21,240
ring-shaped pressure mark
around the edge.

425
00:17:22,790 --> 00:17:24,720
It's identical to the one
on Huo Qicheng's head.

426
00:17:26,030 --> 00:17:28,830
So the killer killed Huo Qicheng

427
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:30,750
and then killed this dog too.

428
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:35,790
If the person who killed
Huo Qicheng and Jin Juan

429
00:17:35,790 --> 00:17:36,720
was the same person,

430
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:39,160
then the killer also killed this dog

431
00:17:39,790 --> 00:17:41,830
to conceal Jin Juan's body.

432
00:17:42,510 --> 00:17:43,310
But

433
00:17:43,590 --> 00:17:45,480
we've been investigating this case

434
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:48,270
on the assumption
that Jin Juan killed Huo Qicheng.

435
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:50,830
Now the real killer used the same weapon

436
00:17:51,030 --> 00:17:52,830
in Jin Juan's case.

437
00:17:56,750 --> 00:17:57,720
I get it.

438
00:17:58,030 --> 00:18:00,270
Jin Juan didn't kill Huo Qicheng.

439
00:18:01,310 --> 00:18:02,830
Someone else did.

440
00:18:02,830 --> 00:18:03,510
Right.

441
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,750
We've been investigating
in the wrong direction all along.

442
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:06,960
I'll notify Captain Qin.

443
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,750
Go.

444
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:11,100
(Longfan Urban Construction General Manager
Huo Qicheng Found Dead in Villa)

445
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:13,480
The dog's autopsy report is out.

446
00:18:13,590 --> 00:18:14,920
The fatal injury was to the head.

447
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:17,400
Its skull was smashed with a hammer.

448
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:18,960
It's identical to

449
00:18:19,110 --> 00:18:21,000
the head injury Huo Qicheng suffered.

450
00:18:22,030 --> 00:18:22,830
Qin.

451
00:18:23,270 --> 00:18:24,790
The Rainy Night Hammer Killer Case

452
00:18:24,790 --> 00:18:25,920
is an unsolved case again.

453
00:18:26,030 --> 00:18:27,640
It's now been merged
with the White-Haired Female Corpse Case.

454
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:28,720
Now

455
00:18:29,270 --> 00:18:30,880
we have to start looking
for the killer all over again.

456
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:32,200
Did you find any signs at the scene

457
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:33,960
of how the bodies were transported?

458
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,030
No.

459
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:36,550
There were no footprints

460
00:18:36,550 --> 00:18:37,750
or tire tracks.

461
00:18:38,830 --> 00:18:41,000
The only useful clue
was a strand of hair

462
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,720
we recovered from the dog.

463
00:18:43,110 --> 00:18:44,350
No traces at all.

464
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,000
Could it be

465
00:18:46,550 --> 00:18:48,790
that the killer carried
the body and the dog

466
00:18:48,830 --> 00:18:50,270
to the burial site by hand?

467
00:18:50,270 --> 00:18:51,590
An adult woman

468
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:53,790
and a large dog
weighing 30 or 40 pounds.

469
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:55,270
Could the killer really

470
00:18:55,750 --> 00:18:57,350
carry one under each arm?

471
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:59,000
You have a point.

472
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:00,070
For one person

473
00:19:00,270 --> 00:19:01,880
to haul two heavy bodies

474
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:03,400
such a long way to bury them

475
00:19:03,920 --> 00:19:05,000
would be far too risky.

476
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:09,000
The starting point and the burial site

477
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,880
must have been very close to each other.

478
00:19:12,350 --> 00:19:13,160
Exactly.

479
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:14,580
Bodies are dumped far away
but buried close by.

480
00:19:14,640 --> 00:19:16,830
The killer chose to dig a pit
instead of dumping them farther away,

481
00:19:16,830 --> 00:19:19,070
which means he considered
this place safe and secure.

482
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:21,200
And given those two heavy loads,

483
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:22,270
that means

484
00:19:22,590 --> 00:19:25,070
the primary scene
of Jin Juan's death can't be far away.

485
00:19:29,590 --> 00:19:30,750
I know where it is.

486
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:32,270
Qin.

487
00:19:32,830 --> 00:19:33,640
This time,

488
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,030
we'll go together.

489
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:36,510
All right.

490
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:45,040
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

491
00:19:48,110 --> 00:19:52,890
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

492
00:19:55,600 --> 00:20:00,980
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

493
00:20:01,510 --> 00:20:06,840
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

494
00:20:08,870 --> 00:20:16,830
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

495
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:22,510
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

496
00:20:24,550 --> 00:20:32,860
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

497
00:20:32,860 --> 00:20:38,710
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

498
00:20:40,170 --> 00:20:48,290
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

499
00:20:48,980 --> 00:20:54,020
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

500
00:20:55,800 --> 00:21:03,840
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

501
00:21:04,120 --> 00:21:11,390
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

502
00:21:11,590 --> 00:21:16,000
♪Can you hear me?♪

503
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:19,800
♪Can you hear me?♪

504
00:21:19,800 --> 00:21:27,260
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

505
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:35,000
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

506
00:21:35,330 --> 00:21:40,940
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

507
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:46,420
♪After all these years♪

508
00:21:48,930 --> 00:21:56,410
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

509
00:21:57,310 --> 00:21:58,610
♪And tell you♪

510
00:21:59,830 --> 00:22:03,100
♪I haven't let you down♪
